  "optionExplanations": {
    "A": "Correct. This is the classic presentation in a young infant with tearing and discharge from birth.",
    "B": "Incorrect. Preseptal cellulitis causes eyelid swelling and erythema, not chronic tearing since birth.",
    "C": "Incorrect. Uveitis is uncommon in this age group and typically presents with photophobia, pain, or redness.",
    "D": "Incorrect. Viral conjunctivitis usually develops after birth and is associated with red, watery eyes rather than symptoms since birth."
